---
import Faq from "../components/Faq.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { breadcrumbLd, faqLd } from "../lib/schema";

const faqs = [
	{
		q: "What does Level 5 wind resistance mean?",
		a: "On DJI’s chart it is roughly 10.7 to 12 m/s sustained. It is a class, not a promise that 12 m/s at 120 m is comfortable. Use the field check against that model’s number.",
	},
	{
		q: "Is Level 4 enough to fly in wind?",
		a: "Level 4 is about 5.5 to 8 m/s. Light consumer quads in that class (Neo, Mini 2 SE, Atom) should treat everyday breezes as the working limit, not a target.",
	},
	{
		q: "Is a higher level always safer?",
		a: "A higher published class usually means a higher ceiling. It does not cancel gusts, rain, or low battery. Compare models on the compare page if you are choosing an airframe for wind.",
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Drone wind resistance levels | Level 4 vs Level 5"
	description="DJI wind resistance levels mapped to m/s, mph, and knots. Level 4 vs Level 5 vs Level 6, and when to stay on the ground."
	jsonLd={[
		breadcrumbLd([
			{ name: "Home", href: "/" },
			{ name: "Wind resistance levels", href: "/drone-wind-resistance-levels" },
		]),
		faqLd(faqs),
	]}
>
	<Header />
	<main class="page-wrap max-w-3xl py-16">
		<p class="font-mono text-caption uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Levels</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-display-lg font-semibold text-ink">Wind resistance levels, decoded.</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-body">
			Consumer drones borrow Beaufort style levels. The table is the useful part; the rest is
			marketing.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-canvas shadow-card">
			<table class="w-full min-w-[28rem] text-left">
				<thead>
					<tr class="bg-canvas-soft font-mono text-caption uppercase text-mute">
						<th class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">Level</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">m/s</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">mph</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">Typical class</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="text-sm text-body">
					<tr class="border-t border-hairline">
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-ink">Level 3</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">3.4–5.4</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">8–12</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">Toy GPS quads</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-t border-hairline">
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-ink">Level 4</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">5.5–8.0</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">12–18</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-neo-wind-resistance-calculator">Neo</a>,{" "}
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-mini-2-se-wind-resistance-calculator">Mini 2 SE</a>,{" "}
							<a class="text-link" href="/potensic-atom-wind-resistance-calculator">Atom</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-t border-hairline">
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-ink">Level 5</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">8.1–10.7 / 12</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">18–24 / 27</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-mini-4-pro-wind-resistance-calculator">Mini 4 Pro</a>,{" "}
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-air-3s-wind-resistance-calculator">Air 3S</a>,{" "}
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-mavic-3-pro-wind-resistance-calculator">Mavic 3 Pro</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-t border-hairline">
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-ink">Level 6</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">12–14</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">27–31</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3">
							<a class="text-link" href="/dji-inspire-3-wind-resistance-calculator">Inspire 3</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<h2 class="mt-12 text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">How to read the number</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-body">
			The level is a bucket. Two Level 5 drones can still differ in grams and in how they handle
			a gust. Treat the m/s figure as the planning cap, then apply a buffer.{" "}
			<a href="/drone-weather" class="text-link">Drone weather</a> is the other half: height and
			gusts, not just the badge on the box.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-6 text-body">
			If your remote shows “Level 5” and the field is gusting past 20 mph at head height, the 120
			m number is worse. Read{" "}
			<a href="/drone-wind-resistance" class="text-link">what wind resistance means</a>, then{" "}
			<a href="/#calculator" class="text-link">run a field check</a>.
		</p>
		<Faq items={faqs} />
		<p class="mt-8">
			<a href="/#calculator" class="font-medium text-link">Open the calculator →</a>
		</p>
		<RelatedLinks
			links={[
				{ href: "/drone-wind-resistance", label: "What wind resistance means" },
				{ href: "/how-it-works", label: "How go / no go is calculated" },
				{ href: "/compare", label: "Compare Mini 4 Pro vs Air 3S" },
				{ href: "/models", label: "Full model database" },
			]}
		/>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
